# Rust Coding Standards

## Error Handling

### In Library Code (omnivore-core)

Use `thiserror` for typed errors:

```rust
use thiserror::Error;

#[derive(Error, Debug)]
pub enum CrawlError {
    #[error("Network error: {0}")]
    Network(#[from] reqwest::Error),

    #[error("Rate limited for domain: {domain}")]
    RateLimited { domain: String },
}
```

### In Application Code (omnivore-cli)

Use `anyhow` for error context:

```rust
use anyhow::{Context, Result};

fn load_config() -> Result<Config> {
    let path = find_config_path()?;
    let content = std::fs::read_to_string(&path)
        .context("Failed to read config file")?;
    toml::from_str(&content)
        .context("Failed to parse config")
}
```

## Async Patterns

```rust
// Use tokio for async
#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> Result<()> {
    // ...
}

// Limit concurrency with semaphores
use tokio::sync::Semaphore;
let semaphore = Arc::new(Semaphore::new(10));
let _permit = semaphore.acquire().await?;
```

## NEVER DO

```rust
// NEVER: unwrap in production
let x = result.unwrap();  // BAD

// NEVER: ignore errors
let _ = fallible_operation();  // BAD

// NEVER: blocking in async
std::fs::read_to_string(path);  // BAD in async context

// NEVER: unsafe without documentation
unsafe { /* ... */ }  // BAD without justification
```

## ALWAYS DO

```rust
// ALWAYS: propagate errors
let x = result?;

// ALWAYS: use async I/O in async contexts
tokio::fs::read_to_string(path).await?;

// ALWAYS: document public APIs
/// Brief description.
///
/// # Errors
/// Returns `Error` when...
pub fn public_function() -> Result<T> { ... }
```

## Import Organization

```rust
// Standard library
use std::collections::HashMap;
use std::sync::Arc;

// External crates
use anyhow::{Context, Result};
use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
use tokio::sync::Semaphore;

// Internal modules
use crate::config::Config;
use crate::error::CrawlError;
```

## Naming Conventions

| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Types | PascalCase | `CrawlConfig` |
| Functions | snake_case | `fetch_page` |
| Constants | SCREAMING_SNAKE | `MAX_RETRIES` |
| Modules | snake_case | `url_frontier` |
